PUBLIC RESPONSE: {25 and 28}

The double-sestina rotation is otherwise flawless through the twelve stanzas and the envoi’s required terminal triad (valleys–music–evening). The single anomaly is inside stanza 5: line 25 supplies the word that belongs in position 3 of the cycle (“forests”) while line 28 supplies the word required for position 4 (“music”). Swapping exactly those two lines restores the mandated 6-1-5-2-4-3 sequence inside the stanza without touching any other terminal word.  

The envoi’s present wording already satisfies the lexical skeleton (valleys / music / evening). Moving line 25 into the envoi would therefore create an unnecessary second “music” line and leave stanza 5 with a missing rotation slot, whereas leaving “These mountains witness shall…” at line 73 preserves both the rhetorical close and the already-correct envoi pattern. All other candidate pairs either violate the rotation or require multiple additional corrections. Hence the transposed lines are 25 and 28.

